    "result_text": "All changes are complete and the test suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## What I changed\n\n**Version-2 identity derivation** \u2014 mixed a fixed `\"V2\"` tag into every identifier so each one changes and no version-1 value recurs:\n- `OwnerIdentity.java` \u2014 added `public static final String VERSION_TAG = \"V2\"` and folded it into the hashed pre-image of `key(...)` (identityKey), `householdIdFor(...)` (householdId) and `memberIdHash(...)` (the memberId's HASH8).\n- `AssignMemberId.java` \u2014 the region code embedded *inside* the memberId is now the plain region + `\"V2\"` (e.g. `NSWV2261A2B3C4D7`).\n\n**Kept the V2 tag out of user-facing fields** \u2014 `CityRegion.localityOfMemberId` reads the plain region back off the prefix via `startsWith(\"NSW\")`, so `locality` stays `\"NSW\"`, `timezone` stays `Australia/Sydney`, and the owner segment's region stays plain (test output confirmed `ownerSegment=STANDARD_METRO`). No code change was needed there beyond the Javadoc, because prefix-matching strips the tag automatically.\n\n**Response shape** (`openapi.yml` + `OwnerMapper.java`):\n- Removed top-level `memberId` / `householdId` / `identityKey`.\n- Added a nested `identity` object (new `OwnerIdentity` schema \u2192 `OwnerIdentityDto`) holding those three.\n- Added top-level integer `apiVersion` = 2.\n- The mapper builds the `identity` group and sets `apiVersion` via expressions.\n\n**Audit event** (`OwnerCreatedEvent.java`) \u2014 moved to schema version 2: added `schemaVersion: 2` and the `ownerSegment` recomputed from the version-2 identity. Emitted JSON now reads:\n`{\"schemaVersion\":2,\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSWV227EB7711C77\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"ownerSegment\":\"STANDARD_METRO\",\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}`\n\nRequest fields are unchanged. The one acceptance test (`coreV2GroupsIdentityAndVersions`) passes, verifying `apiVersion == 2`, the three ids present under `identity`, and absent at top level.\n\nOne interpretation note: the spec's clause \"recompute the owner segment from the version-2 identity\" I implemented by adding the recomputed `ownerSegment` to the v2 audit event (its region derives plain, so it reads `STANDARD_METRO`, not a V2-tagged value). If you intended that clause to mean only that the response's `ownerSegment` field track the new memberId (which it already does automatically), I can drop the segment from the audit JSON.",
