    "probe_text": "Read complete. Here is the full ordered account of `POST /api/owners`, as wired in `owners.POST.yml` and its 16 function classes.\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"` on the whole file. Without that role the request is denied (403) before the pipeline runs.\n\n## The pipeline, in order\n\n**1. `CheckIdempotencyKey`** (entry point)\n- Reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` request header (case-insensitive, trimmed; blank = absent).\n- If the key is present *and* already maps to a live (non-soft-deleted) owner in `IdempotencyStore`: **short-circuits** \u2014 returns that original owner as `200 OK` (re-decorating the DTO with capacityWarning, bulkSignupWarning, possibleDuplicate/possibleDuplicateOf, riskFlag) and the rest of the pipeline never runs.\n- Otherwise (no key, first-seen key, or the stored owner was soft-deleted) it takes the `create` flow into step 2.\n\n**2. `ValidateOwner`** \u2014 binds `@RequestBody` (the one and only body read) and validates. Rejections are all 400:\n- **Address normalization** first: normalizes `addressLine1`/`addressLine2`/flat `address`; the stored `address` is the composed structured form when `addressLine1` is present, else the normalized flat address.\n- **Required-field check** (after normalization): `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` must be non-blank \u2192 else `MissingOwnerFieldsException` listing the offending fields.\n- **Telephone**: normalized to E.164; unnormalizable \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException`. The normalized value is stored.\n- **Email** (optional): when present must match the syntactic pattern (\u2192 `InvalidEmailException`), and its domain must not be on the disposable-domain blocklist (\u2192 `DisposableEmailDomainException`); stored lower-cased/trimmed.\n- **Postcode** (optional): when present must be exactly 4 digits (\u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException`); and if the city maps to a known region, must fall in that region's numeric range (\u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException`); stored trimmed.\n- Publishes the validated/normalized body for later steps.\n\n**3. `CheckIdentityUnique`** \u2014 computes the identity key (SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone|lowerEmail|soundex(lastName)`) and compares against every existing **non-deleted** owner. A match \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (**409**). (Same last name+postcode but different phone is *not* a duplicate here \u2014 it's later flagged as a soft \"possible duplicate.\")\n\n**4. `CheckCityCapacity`** \u2014 counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive, trimmed). If `count >= CityCapacity.MAX_PER_CITY` \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (**409**).\n\n**5. `ResolveRegistrationDate`** \u2014 resolves the effective registration date:\n- Uses the supplied date, or the server's current date if none.\n- A supplied date **after** today \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (**400**); back-dating allowed.\n- Rolls weekends and listed public holidays forward to the next business day.\n- Publishes the adjusted date (drives the daily-limit count, the member-id fiscal year, and the stored `registrationDate`).\n\n**6. `CheckDailyLimit`** \u2014 counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals this adjusted business day. If `count >= 100` (`MAX_PER_DAY`) \u2192 `DailyLimitExceededException` (**429**).\n\n**7. `BuildOwner`** \u2014 maps the validated DTO to a new `Owner` entity and overrides its `registrationDate` with the adjusted date from step 5.\n\n**8. `AssignHousehold`** \u2014 sets `householdId` = first 12 upper-case hex of SHA-256 over normalized `(lastName, postcode)`. No postcode \u2192 no household id. (Scoring only; not duplicate detection.)\n\n**9. `AssignMemberId`** \u2014 assigns `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` (V2 region tag, 2-digit fiscal year of registration, 8-hex hash, Luhn check digit). If the base id collides with an existing owner's `memberId`, de-duplicates by appending `-<n>` (smallest n \u2265 2).\n\n**10. `AssignNamesakeCount`** \u2014 sets `namesakeCount` = number of pre-existing owners sharing this first+last name (case-insensitive). Excludes the new owner (not yet saved).\n\n**11. `SaveOwner`** \u2014 persists the owner via `ownerRepository.save(...)` (assigns its id). **This is the primary write.**\n\n**12. `AuditOwnerCreated`** \u2014 logs a human-readable audit line on the `AUDIT` logger (owner id, memberId, registrationDate, membershipLevel).\n\n**13. `EmitOwnerCreatedEvent`** \u2014 logs a structured JSON `OwnerCreatedEvent` line on the `AUDIT` logger.\n\n**14. `EnqueueWelcomeNotification`** \u2014 logs a welcome line (owner id, memberId) on the `NOTIFY` logger (the \"enqueue\").\n\n**15. `RecordIdempotencyKey`** \u2014 if the request carried an `Idempotency-Key`, records `key \u2192 owner.id` in `IdempotencyStore` so a later repeat resolves in step 1. No-op if no key.\n\n**16. `RespondWithOwnerCreated`** \u2014 builds the `OwnerDto`, decorates it with `capacityWarning`, `bulkSignupWarning`, `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf`, and `riskFlag`, and responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n## Notes\n- **Every step is under `govern: [ transaction ]`** except `validate` (step 2) and `resolveRegistrationDate` (step 5), so the DB work commits once as a unit at the end of the pipeline.\n- **Ordering is deliberate**: validation (400s) precedes the identity/capacity checks (409s) precedes the daily limit (429) precedes any mutation/save \u2014 so a bad body never reaches the duplicate or capacity queries, and nothing is written until all checks pass."
